# The defect, pinned at the replay level, which is the level that would have
# caught it: a one-frame clip at strip index 2 has to draw strip frame 2.
# Before G76 this read 0 -- the first frame of the sheet.
tick 20 /Stage/Fx frame == 2
tick 20 /Stage var:sheet == 2

# And the other number stays itself: the position within a one-frame clip is
# zero, which is what a script comparing against a clip's length wants.
tick 20 /Stage var:within == 0
tick 20 /Stage var:clip == tail

# Before the script switches, the two numbers agree, because `idle` does start
# at the beginning of the strip. That coincidence is why the defect survived.
tick 1 /Stage/Fx frame == 0
